---
import PolicyPage from '../../../components/PolicyPage.astro';
import { DOCUMENTS, isDownloadable } from '../../../lib/documents';

// Look up this document in the manifest — single source of truth
const manifest = DOCUMENTS.find((d) => d.title === 'Privacy & Data Protection');
const pending = manifest ? !isDownloadable(manifest) : true;
const pdfHref = manifest?.file ?? '/documents/privacy-policy.pdf';
---
<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy & Data Protection"
  category="Policy"
  description="How St. Paul's Mission Hospital collects, uses, stores, and protects personal and health information, in line with Kenya's Data Protection Act 2019."
  lastUpdated="2026-01-15"
  version="1.0"
  downloadHref={pdfHref}
  downloadPending={pending}
  contactEmail="dpo@spmh.co.ke"
>

  <h2>Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    St. Paul's Mission Hospital respects your privacy. This policy explains what personal
    and health information we collect, why we collect it, how we protect it, and the
    rights you have over it. It is aligned with the <strong>Kenya Data Protection Act
    2019</strong> and the <strong>Health Act 2017</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Identity data</strong> — name, date of birth, gender, national ID or birth certificate number, photograph (for patient records).</li>
    <li><strong>Contact data</strong> — phone number, postal address, email, next of kin.</li>
    <li><strong>Health data</strong> — medical history, diagnoses, test results, treatment records, prescriptions, imaging, and clinical notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Financial data</strong> — insurance details, SHA number, billing records, payment history.</li>
    <li><strong>Website data</strong> — when you visit newsroom.spmh.co.ke, we may collect standard technical logs (IP address, browser, pages visited). We do not use advertising trackers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>We collect data to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide safe, effective clinical care.</li>
    <li>Maintain accurate medical records, as required by law.</li>
    <li>Process billing and insurance or SHA claims.</li>
    <li>Report to public health authorities, as required by law (for example, notifiable diseases).</li>
    <li>Improve service quality, through anonymized audits and research.</li>
    <li>Communicate with you about appointments, follow-up, and public health information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    We process personal and health data under the following legal bases, as provided by
    the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Consent</strong> — for optional communications and for research participation.</li>
    <li><strong>Contract</strong> — to provide the healthcare services you have requested.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — to comply with health, tax, and public health laws.</li>
    <li><strong>Vital interests</strong> — in a medical emergency where you cannot give consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Public interest</strong> — for public health surveillance and reporting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we store and protect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Electronic records are stored on secure servers with role-based access controls.</li>
    <li>Paper records are kept in locked storage with restricted access.</li>
    <li>All staff receive training on patient confidentiality at induction and annually.</li>
    <li>Access to patient records is logged and auditable.</li>
    <li>Data is backed up regularly, and we maintain a business continuity plan for system failures.</li>
    <li>We do not store patient data on personal devices or unsecured cloud services.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal and health data only when necessary and lawful:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Referral facilities</strong> — when you are referred to another hospital, we share your clinical records with your consent, or in an emergency.</li>
    <li><strong>Insurers and SHA</strong> — for claims processing, limited to what is required for the claim.</li>
    <li><strong>Public health authorities</strong> — for notifiable diseases, as required by Kenyan law.</li>
    <li><strong>Regulators and courts</strong> — when legally compelled.</li>
    <li><strong>Development partners and donors</strong> — only anonymized or aggregated data for reporting, never identifiable patient data.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do <strong>not</strong> sell personal data, and we do not share it for marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Medical records are retained for a minimum of <strong>seven years</strong> after the
    last episode of care, or until a child patient reaches the age of 25, whichever is
    longer. Financial records are retained for <strong>seven years</strong> as required
    by tax law. Website technical logs are retained for <strong>90 days</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> data where we no longer have a legal basis to keep it.</li>
    <li><strong>Restrict</strong> processing in certain circumstances.</li>
    <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing for specific purposes.</li>
    <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, where processing is based on consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Complain</strong> to the Office of the Data Protection Commissioner (ODPC) if you believe your rights have been violated.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact our Data Protection Officer (see below).
    We will respond within <strong>30 days</strong> as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies and website</h2>
  <p>
    The SPMH Newsroom uses essential cookies only. We do not use advertising or
    third-party tracking cookies. Any analytics we collect is aggregated and anonymized.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in law or practice.
    The current version is always available at this page. Material changes will be
    announced on the Newsroom homepage.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Data Protection Officer</strong><br>
    Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@spmh.co.ke">dpo@spmh.co.ke</a><br>
    Post: The Data Protection Officer, St. Paul's Mission Hospital, P.O. Box 426 – Homa Bay, Kenya<br>
    In person: <span style="color:#B26A00;">[SPMH administration office location]</span>
  </div>

  <h2>Complaints to the regulator</h2>
  <p>
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you may lodge a complaint with the
    <strong>Office of the Data Protection Commissioner</strong> at
    <a href="https://www.odpc.go.ke" target="_blank" rel="noopener">odpc.go.ke</a>.
  </p>

</PolicyPage>